WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:36.333
<b>How a person of steady wisdom achieves </b>
<b>complete control over their senses,</b>

2
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:39.041
<b>here, Lord Krishna explains the same.</b>

3
00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:40.166
<b>He says that</b>

4
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:42.083
<b>while an ordinary person</b>

5
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:48.833
<b>can suppress attachments by staying </b>
<b>away from objects that stimulate the senses,</b>

6
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:53.375
<b>these attachments aren't completely eliminated</b>

7
00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:57.083
<b>they're merely suspended temporarily.</b>

8
00:00:57.083 --> 00:01:00.791
<b>They can reawaken later.</b>

9
00:01:00.791 --> 00:01:01.625
<b>However,</b>

10
00:01:01.625 --> 00:01:07.083
<b>for a person of steady wisdom who has </b>
<b>experienced the joy of supreme knowledge,</b>

11
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:12.708
<b>these trivial attachments </b>
<b>cease to exist altogether.</b>

12
00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:26.666
<b>You might wonder anyone can control </b>
<b>their senses to some degree, small or large, </b>

13
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:29.416
<b>so perhaps a person of steady wisdom</b>

14
00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:36.791
<b>is simply more capable of controlling </b>
<b>their senses due to more practice.</b>

15
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:37.791
<b>Here,</b>

16
00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:42.666
<b>we must understand the difference </b>
<b>between these two situations.</b>

17
00:01:42.666 --> 00:01:44.625
<b>An ordinary person</b>

18
00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:51.041
<b>controls themselves merely by staying</b>
<b>away from objects that create desire.</b>

19
00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:52.500
<b>For example,</b>

20
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.625
<b>to improve health, they stay </b>
<b>away from tasty foods.</b>

21
00:01:57.625 --> 00:01:59.500
<b>They restrain themselves.</b>

22
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.375
<b>But their tongue still knows that taste,</b>

23
00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:05.500
<b>still craves it.</b>

24
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.958
<b>There's just a barrier in place.</b>

25
00:02:07.958 --> 00:02:13.833
<b>Once that barrier is removed, the craving </b>
<b>for delicious food will arise again.</b>

26
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:14.666
<b>However,</b>

27
00:02:14.666 --> 00:02:19.083
<b>a person of steady wisdom </b>
<b>doesn't need such barriers.</b>

28
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:23.166
<b>Their sensory cravings </b>
<b>have naturally disappeared.</b>

29
00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:24.166
<b>Because</b>

30
00:02:24.166 --> 00:02:25.958
<b>by attaining supreme knowledge,</b>

31
00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:34.500
<b>they've experienced such joy that </b>
<b>all worldly pleasures pale in comparison.</b>

32
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.000
<b>If a child is playing joyfully in the dirt outside,</b>

33
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.250
<b>you can control them through </b>
<b>scolding or restrictions,</b>

34
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.250
<b>but</b>

35
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.375
<b>their mind still yearns to play.</b>

36
00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:50.958
<b>However,</b>

37
00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:57.666
<b>if from inside the house, mother calls </b>
<b>them to eat their favorite sweet,</b>

38
00:02:57.666 --> 00:03:01.916
<b>the child will instantly abandon </b>
<b>the dirt and run inside.</b>

39
00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:04.916
<b>Here, no control was needed,</b>

40
00:03:04.916 --> 00:03:05.791
<b>because</b>

41
00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:09.416
<b>they received something </b>
<b>so much more enjoyable</b>

42
00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:14.333
<b>that it naturally eliminated</b>
<b>the desire to play in the dirt.</b>

43
00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:18.333
<b>Similarly, a person of steady wisdom </b>
<b>has attained supreme knowledge,</b>

44
00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:22.958
<b>so where is there room for attachments to exist?</b>

45
00:03:22.958 --> 00:03:27.458
<b>Where is there space for </b>
<b>material attachments to survive?</b>

46
00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:36.416
<b>Does this happen to you too?</b>

47
00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:40.583
<b>You try hard to break a bad habit,</b>

48
00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:41.416
<b>but</b>

49
00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:46.250
<b>somehow fall back into the same pattern.</b>

50
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:54.750
<b>And now, self-doubt creeps in, </b>
<b>making you lose faith in your self-control.</b>

51
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.041
<b>The truth is,</b>

52
00:03:57.041 --> 00:04:01.958
<b>once you've experienced a desire,</b>

53
00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:06.708
<b>your mind never truly forgets it.</b>

54
00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:12.250
<b>You can restrain this restless mind temporarily,</b>

55
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.625
<b>but</b>

56
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:21.500
<b>the moment you let go, like a child, </b>
<b>it runs back to that familiar sensation.</b>

57
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.791
<b>So what can be done?</b>

58
00:04:24.791 --> 00:04:28.000
<b>While this wisdom has many layers,</b>

59
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.458
<b>think of it this way:</b>

60
00:04:30.458 --> 00:04:34.250
<b>When does a child give up an old toy?</b>

61
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.958
<b>Only when they find something new to play with.</b>

62
00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:40.208
<b>Similarly,</b>

63
00:04:40.208 --> 00:04:43.458
<b>your restless mind will let go of old habits</b>

64
00:04:43.458 --> 00:04:48.000
<b>only when it embraces new, better ones.</b>

65
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.708
<b>Yes, this requires practice,</b>

66
00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:52.708
<b>but</b>

67
00:04:52.708 --> 00:04:57.166
<b>it's the only path to lasting change.</b>

68
00:04:57.166 --> 00:04:59.500
<b>Take this example</b>

69
00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:07.250
<b>You're addicted to sweets, and your </b>
<b>mind craves that sugary taste.</b>

70
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.250
<b>But</b>

71
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:14.583
<b>processed sweets are harming your health.</b>

72
00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:15.791
<b>In such cases,</b>

73
00:05:15.791 --> 00:05:20.625
<b>completely suppressing your mind's </b>
<b>stubbornness might be difficult.</b>

74
00:05:20.625 --> 00:05:30.250
<b>Instead, satisfy that sweet </b>
<b>craving with natural fruits.</b>

75
00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.208
<b>Yes,</b>

76
00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:34.875
<b>moderation is still needed,</b>

77
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:35.833
<b>but</b>

78
00:05:35.833 --> 00:05:42.666
<b>this is far easier than attempting </b>
<b>to quit sweets entirely.</b>

79
00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:48.041
<b>Gradually, as your mind finds </b>
<b>contentment in fruits,</b>

80
00:05:48.041 --> 00:05:51.583
<b>it will forget the old habit.</b>

81
00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:54.208
<b>The solution isn't restriction,</b>

82
00:05:54.208 --> 00:06:00.500
<b>but redirection towards better alternatives.</b>

83
00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.333
<b>Remember this</b>

84
00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:05.000
<b>it will help in many situations.</b>

85
00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:12.375
<b>Movies here,</b>

86
00:06:12.375 --> 00:06:16.250
<b>provocative music there,</b>

87
00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:23.041
<b>and alluring shows inspired by </b>
<b>western culture everywhere.</b>

88
00:06:23.041 --> 00:06:31.000
<b>The communication revolution has </b>
<b>brought endless temptations into our world.</b>

89
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:36.500
<b>Temptations that could harm children,</b>

90
00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:41.583
<b>derailing them from their purpose.</b>

91
00:06:41.583 --> 00:06:47.583
<b>In today's world, protecting </b>
<b>children from these temptations</b>

92
00:06:47.583 --> 00:06:52.375
<b>has become a real challenge for parents.</b>

93
00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:53.541
<b>But</b>

94
00:06:53.541 --> 00:06:55.541
<b>what's the solution? </b>

95
00:06:55.541 --> 00:07:00.791
<b>Will forcing restrictions help?</b>

96
00:07:00.791 --> 00:07:03.041
<b>Probably not.</b>

97
00:07:03.041 --> 00:07:07.125
<b>It might work temporarily,</b>

98
00:07:07.125 --> 00:07:07.875
<b>but</b>

99
00:07:07.875 --> 00:07:09.666
<b>once the restrictions lift,</b>

100
00:07:09.666 --> 00:07:15.833
<b>children will be even more </b>
<b>drawn to these temptations,</b>

101
00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:23.708
<b>potentially developing resentment </b>
<b>towards their parents.</b>

102
00:07:23.708 --> 00:07:26.291
<b>The answer isn't restriction,</b>

103
00:07:26.291 --> 00:07:27.416
<b>but</b>

104
00:07:27.416 --> 00:07:32.833
<b>redirection towards healthier entertainment.</b>

105
00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:34.416
<b>And remember!</b>

106
00:07:34.416 --> 00:07:36.625
<b>Don't just guide</b>

107
00:07:36.625 --> 00:07:39.958
<b>lead by example.</b>

108
00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:45.208
<b>When parents spend quality time with children</b>

109
00:07:45.208 --> 00:07:46.750
<b>reading books,</b>

110
00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.250
<b>outdoor sports,</b>

111
00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:51.875
<b>artistic activities, and such</b>

112
00:07:51.875 --> 00:07:56.958
<b>when they themselves embrace </b>
<b>these healthy alternatives</b>

113
00:07:56.958 --> 00:08:01.541
<b>and involve their children,</b>

114
00:08:01.541 --> 00:08:11.000
<b>soon enough, kids will naturally drift </b>
<b>away from harmful entertainment.</b>

115
00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:17.583
<b>They'll then spend their free time </b>
<b>only in beneficial activities.</b>

116
00:08:17.583 --> 00:08:19.375
<b>Healthy entertainment</b>

117
00:08:19.375 --> 00:08:22.000
<b>embrace it yourself first,</b>

118
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.416
<b>then inspire your children.</b>

119
00:08:30.083 --> 00:08:37.583
<b>Adapting your habits and </b>
<b>work methods with time</b>

120
00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:42.375
<b>this is crucial in professional life.</b>

121
00:08:42.375 --> 00:08:49.333
<b>There's no guarantee that yesterday's </b>
<b>successful approach will work today.</b>

122
00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:55.625
<b>Yet this creates a dilemma for many.</b>

123
00:08:55.625 --> 00:09:02.416
<b>Changing old habits seems </b>
<b>overwhelmingly difficult.</b>

124
00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:11.791
<b>Often, this happens because people </b>
<b>view the problem from the wrong angle.</b>

125
00:09:11.791 --> 00:09:13.708
<b>They think:</b>

126
00:09:13.708 --> 00:09:15.083
<b>"I'm wrong,</b>

127
00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:16.750
<b>I'm flawed,</b>

128
00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.250
<b>I must change."</b>

129
00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:24.041
<b>Or the complete opposite</b>

130
00:09:24.041 --> 00:09:25.333
<b>"I'm right,</b>

131
00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:28.041
<b>others are wrong."</b>

132
00:09:28.041 --> 00:09:35.250
<b>Both self-blame and blaming </b>
<b>others are negative starting points.</b>

133
00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:37.708
<b>The right mindset is:</b>

134
00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:40.750
<b>Whatever happened was neither right nor wrong,</b>

135
00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:45.708
<b>but now I need a new approach.</b>

136
00:09:45.708 --> 00:09:54.041
<b>Also, look back and remember all those </b>
<b>times when you learned something new,</b>

137
00:09:54.041 --> 00:09:57.583
<b>and it worked.</b>

138
00:09:57.583 --> 00:10:02.291
<b>Move towards new habits with</b>
<b>this positive mindset,</b>

139
00:10:02.291 --> 00:10:05.666
<b>don't curse the old ones.</b>

140
00:10:05.666 --> 00:10:11.416
<b>Surround yourself with similarly</b>
<b>positive-minded people.</b>

141
00:10:11.416 --> 00:10:15.833
<b>Your life will transform before you know it.</b>

